<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siegen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siegen is a university city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the Sieg in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siegerland">Siegerland</a>. Held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-nassau">House of Nassau</a> from the 13th century, it was the residence of the Nassau-Siegen line from 1606, whose Upper and Lower Castles still stand. Long a centre of iron mining and smelting, it was the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-paul-rubens">Peter Paul Rubens</a> in 1577.</p></div>
